# Normalize committed text to LF and check it out as LF everywhere. Without
# this, Windows autocrlf checks files out with CRLF, so the raw-byte SHA-256
# that tools/ci/extract-storage-enums.py pins for the LDD (computed on LF, the
# committed blob) does not match the working copy — G-11 (contract↔LDD)
# then fails LOCALLY on Windows while passing on the Linux CI runner. LF
# everywhere removes that drift. Binary corpus payloads are untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.json.gz binary
